--TEST--
a double-quoted string offers the html literal that prints the same text, keeping its `$name` hole and writing `\"` as `"`, under its own refactor kind, `rule:ide/a-string-converts-to-an-html-template`
--FILE--
<?nvs
var $name = "world";
echo "<p class=\"greeting\">Hello, <|>$name</p>";
--REQUEST--
codeAction
--EXPECT--
3:6-3:46 refactor.rewrite.htmlLiteral Convert to html literal -> "html`<p class="greeting">Hello, $name</p>`"
